# ===== Map B: game modules $049a6-$0a0ff (AI, arrows, demo, puzzle panel,
# ===== mice, board cells, timers, controls/options menus, AI path maps,
# ===== front end, round lifecycle, save file, spawners, input cursor)
#
# Module lifecycle hooks. Every game module exposes up to 6 entry points,
# called in fixed order by these dispatchers:
#   Game_InitModules     (once at program start)          -> *_InitStub / *_Init
#   Game_DeInitModules   (once at program exit)           -> *_DeInit
#   Round_InitModules    (start of Round_Run = a match)   -> *_RoundBegin
#   Round_DeInitModules  (end of Round_Run)               -> *_RoundEnd
#   Round_SetupLevel     (start of every level/round)     -> *_SetupForLevel
#   Round_CleanupLevel   (end of every level/round)       -> *_LevelReset
# Empty ones (just rts) get the suffix "Stub".

# ---------- Round lifecycle dispatchers ----------
F_08664 Game_DeInitModules
@Game_DeInitModules Game_DeInitModules() : program-exit counterpart of Game_InitModules;
@Game_DeInitModules calls the *_DeInit hook of every game module (mostly empty stubs).
F_0873c Round_DeInitModules
@Round_DeInitModules Round_DeInitModules() : end-of-match counterpart of Round_InitModules,
@Round_DeInitModules called once when Round_Run finishes; calls every module's *_RoundEnd hook.
F_08832 Round_CleanupLevel
@Round_CleanupLevel Round_CleanupLevel() : end-of-level counterpart of Round_SetupLevel;
@Round_CleanupLevel calls every module's *_LevelReset hook (Round_Run calls it before
@Round_CleanupLevel setting up the next level, and when the match ends).

