# ---------- AI path maps ($06ec2-$07bb8) ----------
# Path map (640 bytes): +$000 4 x 16 words: for each direction, one bit per column
# of each row (tile visited while moving in that direction); +$080 4 x 128 bytes:
# for each direction, 9 x 12 byte distances (steps). gRocketMaps: 4 players x 3
# maps ($780 per player); map k = paths into the rocket that need k arrows.
F_06ec4 PathMaps_DeInitStub
@PathMaps_DeInitStub PathMaps_DeInitStub() : empty path-maps hook (Game_DeInitModules).
F_06ec6 PathMaps_RoundBeginStub
@PathMaps_RoundBeginStub PathMaps_RoundBeginStub() : empty path-maps hook (Round_InitModules).
F_06ec8 PathMaps_RoundEndStub
@PathMaps_RoundEndStub PathMaps_RoundEndStub() : empty path-maps hook (Round_DeInitModules).
F_06eca PathMaps_BuildForLevel
@PathMaps_BuildForLevel PathMaps_BuildForLevel() : level-start hook (battle modes and cat soccer only).
@PathMaps_BuildForLevel Clears all maps, traces the flow map from every spawner (PathMaps_TraceForward)
@PathMaps_BuildForLevel and builds each player's rocket maps (PathMaps_BuildRocketMaps); sets
@PathMaps_BuildForLevel gPathMapsState = 0 and a table of 5 distance-map pointers.
F_06fb2 PathMaps_LevelResetStub
@PathMaps_LevelResetStub PathMaps_LevelResetStub() : empty path-maps hook (Round_CleanupLevel).
F_07126 PathMaps_TraceForward
@PathMaps_TraceForward PathMaps_TraceForward(a0 = map, d0 = row, d1 = column, d2 = direction,
@PathMaps_TraceForward stack byte = start distance) : follows the way a creature would walk (arrows,
@PathMaps_TraceForward gTurnTable, board wrap), marking bits and shorter distances, up to 144 steps
@PathMaps_TraceForward or until a rocket / an already shorter tile. Builds the flow map from spawners.
F_0727a PathMaps_ClearPlayer
@PathMaps_ClearPlayer PathMaps_ClearPlayer(a0 = player's 3 rocket maps) : clears their bits and distances.
F_072de PathMaps_TraceRocketRight
@PathMaps_TraceRocketRight PathMaps_TraceRocketRight(a0 = player maps, d0 = rocket row, d1 = column) :
@PathMaps_TraceRocketRight if the rocket has no right wall, traces back the tiles that reach it from the
@PathMaps_TraceRocketRight right (asm tracer F_0c9b8). Also runs the C tracer PathMaps_TraceLeftward into
@PathMaps_TraceRocketRight gRocketMapsScratch (result unused, looks like a leftover).
F_0734e PathMaps_TraceRocketLeft
@PathMaps_TraceRocketLeft PathMaps_TraceRocketLeft(a0 = player maps, d0 = row, d1 = column) : same for an
@PathMaps_TraceRocketLeft open left side (F_0c9cc) - but it writes into gRocketMapsScratch instead of a0,
@PathMaps_TraceRocketLeft so the step-by-step rebuild misses this side (apparent original bug).
F_073a8 PathMaps_TraceRocketTop
@PathMaps_TraceRocketTop PathMaps_TraceRocketTop(a0 = player maps, d0 = row, d1 = column) : same for an
@PathMaps_TraceRocketTop open top side (asm tracer F_0c9e0).
F_073e0 PathMaps_TraceRocketBottom
@PathMaps_TraceRocketBottom PathMaps_TraceRocketBottom(a0 = player maps, d0 = row, d1 = column) : same for
@PathMaps_TraceRocketBottom an open bottom side (asm tracer F_0c9f4).
F_07418 PathMaps_BuildRocketMaps
@PathMaps_BuildRocketMaps PathMaps_BuildRocketMaps(a0 = player maps, d0 = rocket row, d1 = column) :
@PathMaps_BuildRocketMaps clears the player's maps then traces back from each open side of the rocket
@PathMaps_BuildRocketMaps (asm tracers F_0c9b8/F_0c9cc/F_0c9e0/F_0c9f4), all in one go.
F_074c2 PathMaps_TraceLeftward
@PathMaps_TraceLeftward PathMaps_TraceLeftward(a0 = maps, d0 = row, d1 = col, d2 = distance, stack w =
@PathMaps_TraceLeftward arrows used 0-2) : C reverse tracer; walks right from (row,col) to mark tiles
@PathMaps_TraceLeftward where a creature moving LEFT reaches the target. Stops on hole, rocket, spawner,
@PathMaps_TraceLeftward other arrow, 144; at walls recurses up/down (natural turn, or +1 arrow).
F_07654 PathMaps_TraceRightward
@PathMaps_TraceRightward PathMaps_TraceRightward(same args) : same as PathMaps_TraceLeftward for creatures
@PathMaps_TraceRightward moving RIGHT (direction 1).
F_077e2 PathMaps_TraceDownward
@PathMaps_TraceDownward PathMaps_TraceDownward(same args) : same for creatures moving DOWN (direction 2).
F_0797c PathMaps_TraceUpward
@PathMaps_TraceUpward PathMaps_TraceUpward(same args) : same for creatures moving UP (direction 3).
F_07b06 PathMaps_ClearTileGrid
@PathMaps_ClearTileGrid PathMaps_ClearTileGrid(a0 = grid) : clears a 9 x 12 grid of 2-byte entries
@PathMaps_ClearTileGrid (used on the grid that follows gRocketMapsScratch).
F_07b48 PathMap_Clear
@PathMap_Clear PathMap_Clear(a0 = map) : clears one 640-byte path map (4 direction bit masks and
@PathMap_Clear 4 distance tables, via F_0c99a / F_0c9a8).
F_07ba8 PathMaps_IsRebuilding
@PathMaps_IsRebuilding PathMaps_IsRebuilding() : d0.w = gPathMapsState (0 idle, 1 rebuild in progress).
@PathMaps_IsRebuilding Ai_Update waits while the maps of its target player are being rebuilt.
F_07bb0 PathMaps_GetRebuildPlayer
@PathMaps_GetRebuildPlayer PathMaps_GetRebuildPlayer() : d0.w = player whose rocket maps
@PathMaps_GetRebuildPlayer Ai_UpdatePathMaps is rebuilding.
B_22114 gPathMapsDirty
@gPathMapsDirty gPathMapsDirty.b : set by Arrow_Create; Ai_UpdatePathMaps then starts a rebuild.
B_2393c gFlowMap
@gFlowMap gFlowMap (640 bytes) : path map of the tiles walked by creatures leaving the spawners.
B_23bbc gRocketMaps
@gRocketMaps gRocketMaps[4][3] (640 bytes each) : per player, tiles that lead into his rocket
@gRocketMaps with 0, 1 or 2 arrows (Ai_GetRocketMap).
B_259bc gRocketMapsScratch
@gRocketMapsScratch gRocketMapsScratch[4][3] : second set of rocket maps written by
@gRocketMapsScratch PathMaps_TraceRocketRight/Left and never read by the AI.
B_27894 gPathMapsState
@gPathMapsState gPathMapsState.w : 0 idle, 1 rebuilding (next word = step 0-6 of the rebuild).
B_27898 gPathMapsPlayer
@gPathMapsPlayer gPathMapsPlayer.w : player 0-3 whose rocket maps are being rebuilt.

# ---------- Front end menus ($07bb8-$08600) ----------
F_07bb8 FrontEnd_Init
